# Files that must never enter the published archive.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS
# --------------------
# 0.5.5 shipped a 2.1 MB archive containing `build/` — including a Flutter
# kernel cache (`build/test_cache/.../*.cache.dill.track.dill`) that embedded
# 465 absolute paths from the maintainer's machine. Consumers who pulled 0.5.5
# downloaded all of it.
#
# The cause was NOT a missing .gitignore rule. The repo-root .gitignore has
# ignored `**/build/` since 2026-03-04, and `dart pub publish` honours it when
# run from inside the work tree. But 0.5.5 was published from a staging copy
# OUTSIDE the git work tree, and a repo-root .gitignore does not travel with a
# copied package directory. Pub then included everything on disk — and reported
# "0 warnings" while doing it.
#
# `.pubignore` lives inside the package, so it travels wherever the package is
# copied, staged, or archived. It holds in exactly the condition where the
# repo-root .gitignore silently stops applying.
#
# Do not delete this file to "clean up". It is the countermeasure.

# Build output (the 0.5.5 defect).
build/

# Tooling / analysis artifacts.
.dart_tool/
coverage/
doc/api/

# Library packages do not ship a lockfile; consumers resolve their own.
pubspec.lock

# Scratch.
*.log
